ll pending specs; and then there's the larger utilities like wc and the ls variants that are spec-complete but haven't been implemented yet.\n\nSince release 00.0 is essentially complete (the existing code for format, sys, and testutils covers it, and magefiles is excluded from generation anyway), I should focus on the earliest incomplete release, which means starting with 01.1 and picking cat as the next task to implement. DD7). The only generation target is cmd/version.\n- uc002-format: code already exists in source_code\n- uc003-sys: code already exists in source_code  \n- uc004-testutils: code already exists in source_code\n\nSo effectively 00.0 is done (or not actionable). The next release is 01.1 (cat).\n\nFor cat, I need to look at what specs exist. The analysis says rel01.1-uc001-cat has spec_complete status but code not started. I need to read the PRD... but I can't read files (constraint says not to). However, I need to know what the PRD says to create a proper task.\n\nWait, looking more carefully at what's available: the source_code section only includes pkg/ files. There's no cmd/cat code shown. The implementation_status says cmd/cat has spec complete (rel01.1), code at generation-merged tags. So code exists at a tag but not on the working branch.\n\nBut the constraint says: \"When source_code contains .go files for a package, that package already exists.\" The source_code section doesn't contain any cmd/cat files, so it doesn't exist on the current branch.\n\nHowever, there's a problem - I don't have the PRD content for cat. The project_context doesn't include it inline. The required_reading for the task should point to the PRD file so the stitch agent can read it. For cmd/cat, I know it's a coreutils utility with a PRD at docs/specs/product-requirements/ and a use case at docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-, but I need to reference those files so the agent can access the actual specifications.\n\nI'm stuck on the PRD numbering without being able to read the